erm`.\n- **Why there is no chair:** The bill forbids school or district policies that keep a student's education record from parents. It also bars changing the record's gender identity \"without written parental consent\". That puts him against rungs 1 and 2. But the bill doesn't require schools to notify parents (rung 4), and it doesn't cover staff using a different name or pronouns (rung 5). Its record-access provision doesn't match rung 3 (\"tell parents when parents ask\") clause for clause either. So the evidence shows which side he is on but doesn't pick a rung.\n- **Fields:** Both passages are coded as one vote record, using the codebook's two-passage format. The provision quote is on the bill-text passage, and the actor and tally quotes are on the vote page. I listed no extra sources to fetch and no quotes, because none of the sources contain his own words.\n\n**Connector status:** The GitHub connector failed to connect. These claude.ai connectors still need authorizing in claude.ai connector settings: Benevity, Candid, Canva, Figma, Givebutter, Harvey and WorkOS. None of them were needed for this task.","ttft_ms":15914,"type":"result","duration_ms":37404,"uuid":"2f36d4b5-5253-43c0-a6f7-9d3fe9d0c837","ttft_stream_ms":7548,"time_to_request_ms":169,"first_content_frame_ms":7548,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
